WEBVTT

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-1/0
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:10.714
<v Dana Whitcombe>Morning everyone, can you hear me? I think I'm on mute. Okay, now.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-2/0
00:00:11.914 --> 00:00:21.343
<v Priya Raman>Yes we can hear you. Sorry, I'm in the car park, give me a second to find somewhere quiet.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-3/0
00:00:22.543 --> 00:00:33.614
<v Dana Whitcombe>No rush. Okay, the agenda is the cutover plan, the scanner order, and the training. Let's start with the cutover.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-4/0
00:00:34.814 --> 00:00:46.671
<v Marcus Bell>So the cutover. We agreed last time on a single weekend, but the carrier says they can't take the extra pallets on the 22nd.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-5/0
00:00:47.871 --> 00:00:53.086
<v Dana Whitcombe>Right. So what are the options?</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-6/0
00:00:54.286 --> 00:01:02.357
<v Marcus Bell>Two phases. Chilled goods first on the 22nd, ambient the weekend after.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-7/0
00:01:03.557 --> 00:01:11.771
<v Tomasz Kowal>That works for me, the ambient racking isn't ready until the 28th anyway.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-8/0
00:01:12.971 --> 00:01:21.829
<v Dana Whitcombe>Okay, let's do that then. Two phases, chilled on the 22nd and ambient on the 29th.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-9/0
00:01:23.029 --> 00:01:30.743
<v Elena Sosa>Sorry to interrupt, my dog is going mad at the postman. I'll mute.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-10/0
00:01:31.943 --> 00:01:39.586
<v Dana Whitcombe>Ha, fine. Marcus, can you confirm the new dates with the carrier?</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-11/0
00:01:40.786 --> 00:01:46.643
<v Marcus Bell>Yes, I'll confirm with them by Thursday.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-12/0
00:01:47.843 --> 00:01:52.914
<v Dana Whitcombe>Great. Next, scanners. Priya?</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-13/0
00:01:54.114 --> 00:02:06.043
<v Priya Raman>We ordered forty handheld scanners. The supplier says delivery is the first week of December. Which is after the first phase.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-14/0
00:02:07.243 --> 00:02:15.314
<v Dana Whitcombe>Hmm. That's a problem then, the chilled team need scanners on the 22nd.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-15/0
00:02:16.514 --> 00:02:26.514
<v Priya Raman>I could chase them. Actually no, Elena has the relationship with the supplier, it should be Elena.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-16/0
00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:34.857
<v Elena Sosa>Back. Fine, I'll call them tomorrow and ask for ten early.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-17/0
00:02:36.057 --> 00:02:45.486
<v Tomasz Kowal>If they can't, we can use the old ones from the Leeds site. They're ancient but they work.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-18/0
00:02:46.686 --> 00:02:57.186
<v Marcus Bell>I can collect the old scanners from Leeds. Actually no, I'm off from the 17th. Scrap that, somebody else.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-19/0
00:02:58.386 --> 00:03:06.171
<v Dana Whitcombe>Let's park the Leeds idea as plan B. Nobody needs to act on it yet.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-20/0
00:03:07.371 --> 00:03:14.943
<v Priya Raman>Training next. The agency wants numbers by the end of next week.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-21/0
00:03:16.143 --> 00:03:20.857
<v Dana Whitcombe>How many people is that?</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-22/0
00:03:22.057 --> 00:03:28.986
<v Tomasz Kowal>Thirty-two on chilled. I think. Don't quote me on that.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-23/0
00:03:30.186 --> 00:03:38.043
<v Priya Raman>I'll send the agency the numbers once Tomasz confirms the headcount.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-24/0
00:03:39.243 --> 00:03:44.886
<v Tomasz Kowal>I'll get you the headcount by Monday.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-25/0
00:03:46.086 --> 00:03:54.800
<v Dana Whitcombe>Also, heads up on budget. Finance has cut the contingency from 15 to 10 percent.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-26/0
00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:05.143
<v Priya Raman>That's tight. If the scanners are late and we need to rent some, we'd blow through it.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-27/0
00:04:06.343 --> 00:04:11.271
<v Dana Whitcombe>Yes, one to keep an eye on.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-28/0
00:04:12.471 --> 00:04:22.043
<v Marcus Bell>Related, the carrier's booking portal has been down since Friday so I can't even book slots.</v>

a3f1c2d4-5b6e-47a8-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d-29/0
00:04:23.243 --> 00:04:30.386
<v Dana Whitcombe>Noted. Anything else? No? Thanks all, same time next week.</v>

